# .cbmignore — paths codebase-memory-mcp should not index.
#
# The graph already honours the .gitignore hierarchy, so this file is only for
# things that are COMMITTED but not worth indexing, plus a defensive secrets
# pass. The secrets pass matters more than it looks: the index stores no file
# contents, but snippet retrieval reads from disk at query time using stored
# line numbers — so an indexed credential file becomes a credential reader for
# anything driving the MCP server, subagents included.
#
# The line drawn here, deliberately: credential MATERIAL is excluded;
# environment DATA is kept. agent-cloud is a public repo whose whole design is
# that real IPs and credentials live in the private site-config repo, so the 29
# .j2 templates and 4 platform/inventory/*.yml files here carry {{ placeholders }}
# by construction. They are also the most structurally valuable content in the
# repo — they define how every service gets configured — so they are INDEXED on
# purpose, not excluded by reflex.

# --- memory/tooling stores (they index themselves otherwise) ---
.codebase-memory/
.remember/
graphify-out/
.worktrees/

# --- test scaffolding: high volume, low structural signal ---
**/testdata/
**/fixtures/
**/__snapshots__/
**/*.generated.*
*.min.js

# --- Python (pyproject.toml, ruff + pytest) ---
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Go ---
vendor/
bin/

# --- Terraform / HCL policies ---
.terraform/
*.tfstate*

# --- secrets pass: credential material only ---
# netbox-docker/ (a vendored upstream clone carrying env/*.env) is already
# gitignored, so it never reaches the index; these patterns are the guard for
# the NEXT untracked credential file that is not yet ignored.
secrets/
**/secrets/
*.env
**/credentials.json
*.key
*.pem
*_rsa
*_ed25519

# --- vendored upstream clone ---
# netbox-docker/ is a nested git clone of the upstream netbox-docker project.
# It IS gitignored (platform/services/netbox/deployment/.gitignore), but the
# graph does NOT honour that nested ignore — verified: a clean delete_project +
# re-index still returned all 41 of its files in the File list. Indexing them
# would make upstream third-party CI scripts and Django config answer "what
# calls what" as if they were ours. Excluded explicitly.
platform/services/netbox/deployment/netbox-docker/
netbox-docker/
